@

A save refused for want of the lock keeps the session in a file beside
its own (\cref{sec:session-lock} in the review chapter), and nothing
reads that file until someone merges it.  So the list names such
files, also when there is no session to list, and says how to merge
them; the kept file's name ends in a time and a random part, not in
[[.json]], so it is never listed as a session itself.

<<sessions command>>=
def warn_about_unsaved_sessions() -> None:
    """Name the files of refused saves on stderr, if there are any."""
    from scholar.review import unsaved_session_files

    kept = unsaved_session_files()
    if kept:
        Console(stderr=True).print(
            f"[yellow]Warning:[/yellow] {len(kept)} file(s) hold a "
            "session that a save could not write to its session file: "
            f"{escape(', '.join(path.name for path in kept))}. Merge each "
            "into its session with `scholar sessions recover FILE`, or "
            "delete it with `scholar sessions recover FILE --discard`."
        )
