\paragraph{Decisions on records without an abstract.}
How many decisions rest on a title alone, and whether anyone looked for
the abstract, is a question about the whole session
(\url{https://github.com/dbosk/scholarcli/issues/293}), so
[[sessions show]] answers it in one line after the quote check, not per
paper: the report's sentence ([[decided_without_abstract_sentence]],
\cref{sec:abstract-lookup} in the review module), printed when some
decided paper has no abstract.  The JSON form gives each decision its
[[abstract_lookup]] record when it has one, and the counts at the top
level under [[decided_without_abstract]], also only when there is such
a paper, so the JSON of a session without one is as it was.

