[[export_failure_text]] words the message from the error.  Only an
[[OutputsNotPlaced]] can have changed a file, and only when its
[[changed]] is true; every other error came before the first move.
With [[recorded_draw]] (\cref{sec:rest-sample-sheet} has why the session is
saved before the files are moved) the first line says that the draw was
recorded, which is a change to the session, so the line about the files
names the exported files rather than claiming that no file at all was
written.

<<sessions command>>=
def export_failure_text(error: Exception, recorded_draw: bool = False) -> str:
    """What a failed export says, from what its files hold now."""
    from scholar.utils import OutputsNotPlaced

    placing = isinstance(error, OutputsNotPlaced)
    reason = error.reason if placing else f"{type(error).__name__}: {error}"
    changed = placing and error.changed
    rolled_back = placing and error.rolled_back
    if changed:
        lead = (
            "Export failed after the draw was recorded and could not be "
            "rolled back" if recorded_draw
            else "Export failed part-way and could not be rolled back"
        )
        return "\n".join([f"{lead}: {reason}", *error.file_lines()])
    if recorded_draw:
        return (f"Export failed after the draw was recorded: {reason}\n"
                "None of the exported files was written or changed"
                + ("; the moves were rolled back." if rolled_back else "."))
    return ("Export failed" + (" and was rolled back" if rolled_back else "")
            + f", no files were written or changed: {reason}")
@

The regression test makes the \LaTeX{} step fail after it has already
written its [[.bib]], over an earlier complete export.  The earlier
[[.csv]], [[.bib]] and [[.tex]] must survive byte for byte, no staging
directory may be left behind, and the user gets one line, not a
traceback.

