\paragraph{A CSV for a spreadsheet program.}
\label{sec:export-spreadsheet-safe}
[[sessions export -f csv --spreadsheet-safe]] (or [[-f all]]) writes
the CSV through [[SpreadsheetSafeWriter]]
(\cref{sec:spreadsheet-safe} in the review module, which gives the
reference, the characters, the prefix and its limits): every text cell
that begins with a character a spreadsheet program may read as the
start of a formula, or with the quote, gets one [[']] in front; a
number in the [[year]] and [[llm_confidence]] columns is left as it
is, and anything else there is treated as text.  It
takes the help text, the [[None]] default and the one-line switch of
[[search]]'s flag (\cref{sec:search-csv-spreadsheet-safe}).  The
\LaTeX{} report, the audit table and the screen sheet are not CSV, so
the flag with one of them alone would be ignored; like the screen
sheet's options it is refused before the session is read.

