\paragraph{A sheet for the first screen.}
\label{sec:first-screen-sheet}
The sheet above is for a second screen, so it lists decided papers.
But most screening by agents is the first screen: the pending records,
decided with [[sessions decide --reasons-file]], and that is where the
defaulted batches of \cref{sec:decide-batch-check} were seen.  So
[[--pending]] lists the papers whose decision is pending instead, one
line per paper id (a copy under the same id once, as above), with the
same columns and the same cleaning.  No verdict exists for them, so
nothing can give one away.  It cannot be combined with [[--sample]]
or [[--undecided-by]], which select decided papers for a second
screen; that is a usage error before the session is read.  With
[[--batch-size]] the pending papers are cut into sheets as the decided
ones are (\cref{sec:sheet-batches}), and a screener's reasons file that
keeps its sheet's [[# batch:]] line can be checked against the sheet
([[--sheet]], \cref{sec:batch-against-sheet}).

