    assert result.exit_code == 1
    assert "None of the 5 pending papers is in the tier" in " ".join(
      result.output.split())
@

\paragraph{A sample of the rest.}
\label{sec:rest-sample-sheet}
A tier says what was screened, but nothing about what it left out;
the issue that asked for this
(\url{https://github.com/dbosk/scholarcli/issues/315}) reports a
literature look by the author that found a fixed place cut to be no
stopping rule.  What a review
can state about the rest is an estimate from a random sample of it,
screened like the tier.  [[--rest-sample N --seed S]], given with
[[--pending]] and the tier options, lists such a sample on the sheet
instead of the tier: [[N]] of the pending papers the tier leaves out,
drawn as [[llm sample]] draws ([[draw_tier_sample]],
\cref{sec:tier-sample} in the LLM review module), in the order drawn;
when the rest holds no more than [[N]], all of it, a census.  The
counts of the tier are printed and written to [[BASE-tier.json]] as
for the tier itself, with the draw beside them, and [[--batch-size]]
cuts the sample into sheets as it cuts any sheet; the batch ids differ
from the tier's, since the papers do.

The draw is recorded in the session ([[TierSample]],
\cref{sec:tier-sample-record} in the review module), so that the sample
can be reported once it is screened ([[sessions tier-sample]], below)
and repeated from its seed.  So, unlike every other export, this one
saves the session; the help says so.  It keeps a copy of the session
file first ([[keep_copy_before_run]], as the other writing commands
do), and it saves inside the staging of the export: an export that
fails before the save writes neither the sheet nor the record, and a
failed save writes no sheet, so a sheet never lists a sample the
session does not record.  [[--dry-run]] draws in memory and prints the
counts and what would be written, writing nothing.

The options are checked before the session is read, as the other
options of the sheet are.  The rest is defined only by a tier, of
pending papers: the sample needs [[--pending]] and at least one tier
option.  A random sample needs a seed; there is no default, since a
default seed would be no choice.  [[--seed]] and [[--dry-run]] mean
nothing without [[--rest-sample]] and are refused alone.

