    console.print(escape(rest_draw_line(rest_draw)), soft_wrap=True)
    console.print("The draw is recorded in the session.")
@

The session is saved inside the staging, before the staged files are
moved into place, so a failure of that move leaves a recorded draw
without its sheet.  The other order, the files first and the session
last, would leave a sheet whose draw a failed save did not record; its
papers would be screened from it and so stop being pending, and the
same seed would then draw other papers, so that sample could never be
recorded.  A recorded draw without a sheet loses nothing: [[sessions
tier-sample]] lists its papers and [[llm classify --tier-sample]] takes
them.  So the export saves first, and once it has saved, a failure says
so: the draw's id, that it is recorded, what became of the exported
files, and where its papers are listed.  The files are moved all or
nothing as far as the file system allows (\cref{sec:staged-outputs}),
so the sheet was not written unless putting a file back failed too; in
that case the message lists what each file holds and leaves the sheet
to that list.

A save can also be refused: when another process holds the session's
lock past the wait, [[save_session]] writes nothing to the session,
keeps this process's session beside it and raises [[SessionNotSaved]]
(\cref{sec:session-lock} in the review module); the pre-run copy takes
the same lock and is refused the same way, before anything is kept.
The error passes on to [[main]], which prints its one line (with the
kept file and the [[sessions recover]] command that merges it), not
the export's own message: the staging is discarded, so no sheet and no
tier file are written, and nothing claims that a draw was recorded.  A
later [[sessions recover]] of the kept file adds the draw to the
session, since the kept file holds the session as a save would have
written it, [[tier_samples]] included.  The draw then has no sheet;
[[sessions tier-sample]] lists its papers.  When the pre-run copy is
refused, nothing is kept and nothing is recorded: the export can simply
be run again, and with the same seed and the same pending papers it
draws the same papers.

<<say that the draw is recorded although the export failed>>=
