\paragraph{Reporting a sample of the rest.}
\label{sec:sessions-tier-sample}
[[scholar sessions tier-sample S]] lists the draws a session records
(\cref{sec:rest-sample-sheet}): per draw its id, date, seed and rule,
how many papers were drawn of how many outside the tier, how many of
them have been screened, by anyone, and how many of those bear on the
question, by the rule of the audit table ([[tier_sample_counts]],
\cref{sec:tier-sample-record} in the review module).  With
[[--report]] it adds the rate, its 95\,\% modified Wilson interval and
the sentence a method can quote ([[tier_sample_report]] and
[[tier_sample_sentence]], \cref{sec:tier-sample} in the LLM review
module); while part of the draw is unscreened, or a drawn paper is not
found, the rate is withheld and the reason given instead, and the
papers not yet screened are listed for [[sessions decide]] or [[llm
classify --tier-sample]].  It is read-only and exits~0 whatever it
finds; [[-f json]] gives the same for a script.

The help says what the estimate is and is not, since the number will
be quoted: the share of bearing records among those the tier left out,
as judged by whoever screened the sample; not which records they are,
and not, when the sample holds none, that the rest holds none.

<<sessions command>>=
@sessions_app.command("tier-sample")
def sessions_tier_sample(
    name: Annotated[
        str,
        typer.Argument(
            help="Session name or query whose samples of a tier's rest "
                 "to list.",
            autocompletion=complete_session_name,
        ),
    ],
    report: Annotated[
        bool,
        typer.Option(
            "--report",
            help="Add the rate of bearing records, its 95% modified "
                 "Wilson interval and a sentence for a method section.",
        ),
    ] = False,
    output_format: Annotated[
        str,
        typer.Option(
            "--format", "-f",
            help="Output format: table or json.",
            autocompletion=complete_display_format,
        ),
    ] = "table",
) -> None:
    """
    List the samples drawn from the pending papers a screening tier left
    out (`sessions export -f screen-sheet --rest-sample N --seed S`).

    For each draw: how many papers were drawn of how many outside the
    tier, how many of them have been screened (decided, by anyone) and
    how many of those bear on the question (cited, or kept as supporting
    or qualifying the claim, as the audit table counts them). With
    --report, the share of bearing records among the screened, its 95%
    modified Wilson interval (as `llm sample --report` gives it) and one
    sentence for a method section; while part of the draw is unscreened
    or a drawn paper is not found, no rate is given and the reason is.

    The rate estimates the share of bearing records among all the
    records the tier left out, as judged by whoever screened the
    sample. It does not say which records they are, and a sample in
    which none bears does not show that none does: the interval's upper
    end says how far the share may reach. Read-only; exits 0.
    """
    from scholar.llm_review import tier_sample_report, tier_sample_sentence
    from scholar.review import (
        tier_sample_counts, tier_sample_counts_text, tier_sample_data,
    )

    if output_format not in ("table", "json"):
        Console().print(
            f"[red]Unknown format: {escape(output_format)}; use table or "
            "json.[/red]"
        )
        raise typer.Exit(2)
    session = open_session_argument(name)
    if session is None:
        Console().print(f"[red]Session not found: {escape(name)}[/red]")
        raise typer.Exit(1)
    rows, counts_texts = [], []
    for draw in session.tier_samples:
        counts = tier_sample_counts(session, draw)
        counts_texts.append(tier_sample_counts_text(counts))
        data = tier_sample_data(draw, counts)
        if report:
            <<add the rate of a draw to its data>>
        rows.append(data)
    if output_format == "json":
        print(json.dumps(rows, indent=2))
        return
    <<print the samples of a tier's rest>>
