\paragraph{Classifying a sample of the rest.}
A drawn sample is screened like the tier, by a human, an agent or the
classifier.  [[llm classify --tier-sample ID]] hands the classifier the
pending papers of that draw only, as [[--top]] hands it a tier
(\cref{sec:llm-classify-tier}): through the [[candidates]] of
[[classify_papers_with_llm]], with the session's examples and
vocabulary; [[-n]] still caps the run.  A drawn paper already decided
is not classified again, and a paper not found in the session is
skipped, as the report counts it.  The id is the one [[sessions
tier-sample]] and [[sessions show]] print; an unknown id is a usage
error naming the draws the session holds.  The option selects pending
papers, so it is refused with [[--second-screen]], and with the tier
options, which select another set.

