A sheet made for a review sample is not blind to what the sample
itself tells: one drawn from discards only ([[llm sample
--discarded]]) puts only discards on the sheet, and one drawn by
confidence tells each paper's range of confidence.  The TUI's blind
mode says so when it starts, and the sheet says the same, with the same
lines ([[sample_giveaway]], \cref{sec:sample-giveaway} in the review
module), on standard error, so that whoever hands the sheet to a
screener knows what it gives away.  A sheet of every decided paper
draws on no sample and gets no line.

