The sheets in batches (\cref{sec:sheet-batches}) are checked on the same
session.  Cut into sheets of two, its three papers give two sheets and
a manifest; each sheet starts with its three comment lines, and below
them the header and rows are those of the single sheet, cut in order.
A second export gives the same ids, another size other ids, and the
manifest reads back with [[csv]] even when the base name starts with a
quote mark.  A sheet
then goes round the loop: a reasons file that keeps the sheet's
[[# batch:]] line is given to [[sessions decide]] with the sheet, the
batch id is stored with each decision, and the sheet is all returned.

