The tests above name the source, as every script must now.  The next
ones check who is recorded when the source is left out, the agent
source, and the tags of a decision that overturns an earlier one.
CliRunner gives the command a standard input that is not a terminal,
which is exactly the agent's situation.  The terminal case needs a real
terminal, so that test runs the command in a subprocess whose standard
input is a pseudo-terminal: the code under test then asks the operating
system, as it does for the user, instead of a patched answer.

