\paragraph{A dry run of a decision.}
[[sessions decide --dry-run]] runs everything a real run runs up to the
save: the line checks, the id resolution, the copy and conflict rules,
the quote check and the batch check, and their refusals with the same
exit codes, so that a screener, or a validator outside Scholar, can ask
Scholar whether a batch would pass instead of reimplementing its
checks (\url{https://github.com/dbosk/scholarcli/issues/291}).  It then
records the decisions in memory only, so that what it reports (the
tags no paper had, the papers counted) is what the real run would
report, says what it would have recorded, and writes nothing: no save,
and no line that says the batch was saved.  [[sessions decide]] keeps
no copy of the session before a run, so there is no copy to skip.

