Let's check both on invented sessions.  A reasons file of two
concatenated batches, each of thirty honest lines, of which the second
gives every line 0.85, is not flat as a whole: only its batch shows the
one confidence, under its id, and [[--strict]] refuses it.  The ids are
stored per line and shown by [[sessions show -f json]].  [[--batch]]
goes with [[--reason]], is refused without a reason, with a file that
names its batches, and when too long.  A sheet of ten records answered
by seven of them and one record not on it is reported both ways, saved
without [[--strict]] and refused with it; a sheet that lists no id is a
usage error.  [[sessions screen]] stores the batch of a verdicts file's
