\paragraph{Records decided without an abstract.}
\label{sec:decided-without-abstract}
Records were screened before [[scholar enrich]] had been run, so that
their verdicts rest on titles alone, and nothing said so
(\url{https://github.com/dbosk/scholarcli/issues/293}).  So whenever a
machine or an agent records verdicts ([[sessions decide --source]]
[[agent]] or [[llm]], [[sessions screen --as]] [[agent]] or [[llm]],
[[llm classify]] with or without [[--second-screen]]), the command
prints one line on standard error when some of the records it decided
or screened have no abstract: how many of how many, split by what the
last enrichment found for them ([[abstract_gap]],
\cref{sec:abstract-lookup} in the review module), and the hint to run
[[scholar enrich]] first.  Records whose abstract is doubtful
(\cref{sec:fetched-abstract} in the review module) are counted at the
end of the line, since a decision on one rests on the title too.  The
hint is given only when it can help: when a lookup failed, there is no
record of one, or an abstract is doubtful, which [[scholar enrich]]
judges and replaces when a source has a real one; a record every
source answered without an abstract, or one without a DOI, would get
the same answer again.  It names [[--pending-only]] only where the
records counted are still pending, on a dry run and after [[sessions
screen]], which changes no decision: after a real [[decide]], [[llm
classify]] or a second screen of decided papers they are not, and
[[--pending-only]] would skip exactly them.  It agrees in number with
its counts (\enquote{1 of the 3 records decided has no abstract}).
It is a warning and nothing more: a review
may have a rule for records without an abstract, and the screener may
be applying it.  A human's decisions get no such line, since a human at
the TUI or the terminal sees the record in front of them.  A dry run
says \enquote{selected} instead of \enquote{decided}, since nothing is.
The session is named as the user types it ([[session_argument]]),
quoted for the shell.

<<sessions command>>=
def abstract_gap_line(
    gap, argument: str, verb: str, *, pending: bool
) -> str | None:
    """The line on records `verb` (decided, screened) without an abstract.

    None when every record has an abstract (and none is doubtful). The
    hint names `--pending-only` only when the records are `pending`.
    """
    import shlex

    from scholar.review import abstract_gap_parts

    def has(count: int) -> str:
        return "has" if count == 1 else "have"

    if not gap.without and not gap.doubtful:
        return None
    parts = abstract_gap_parts(gap)
    records = "record" if gap.papers == 1 else "records"
    if gap.without:
        line = (f"{gap.without} of the {gap.papers} {records} {verb} "
                f"{has(gap.without)} no abstract")
        if parts:
            line += f" ({'; '.join(parts)})"
        if gap.doubtful:
            line += f", and {gap.doubtful} {has(gap.doubtful)} a doubtful one"
    else:
        line = (f"{gap.doubtful} of the {gap.papers} {records} {verb} "
                f"{has(gap.doubtful)} a doubtful abstract")
    if gap.failed or gap.no_record or gap.doubtful:
        only = " --pending-only" if pending else ""
        line += (
            f"; run `scholar enrich {shlex.quote(argument)}{only} "
            "--fields abstract` first if that has not been tried"
        )
    return line + "."


def print_abstract_gap(
    decisions, session, verb: str, *, pending: bool
) -> None:
    """Print `abstract_gap_line` for `decisions` on stderr, if any."""
    from scholar.review import abstract_gap, session_argument

    line = abstract_gap_line(
        abstract_gap(decisions), session_argument(session), verb,
        pending=pending,
    )
    if line:
        Console(stderr=True).print(
            f"[yellow]{escape(line)}[/yellow]", soft_wrap=True,
            highlight=False,
        )
