\subsection{Retiring a search}
\label{sec:sessions-retire-search}

A session keeps every search that was run with [[-n]], drafts and
malformed attempts included, and the reports counted them all, so the
audit caption disagreed with the review's method text
(\url{https://github.com/dbosk/scholarcli/issues/275}).
[[sessions retire-search]] marks search records as retired
([[retire_record]], \cref{sec:retired-searches} of the review module,
which explains why the record and its links stay); the reports then
count the current searches and state the retired ones apart.  It is
built like [[sessions reset]] (\cref{sec:sessions-reset}): the session
is opened with [[open_session_argument]], option errors exit with
status~2 before it is loaded, a selector that matches nothing exits
with status~1 and saves nothing, [[--dry-run]] lists what would change
and writes nothing, and otherwise the file is first copied under the
label [[pre-retire-search]] ([[keep_copy_before_run]]) and every record
of the run gets one time from the review module's clock seam
[[_utcnow]], with [[--note]] and [[--by]] as given.

Records are selected in one of three ways.
\begin{description}
\item[[[--query]]] The exact query string, as [[sessions show]] prints
  it, narrowed by [[--provider]].  One query run with two filter sets
  is two searches (\cref{sec:search-record-key} of the review module),
  and retiring both by their words alone may not be what was meant, so
  a match of records with different filters is refused (status~2),
  naming them with their ids, unless [[--filters-like]] narrows it
  to text found in the record's flags as [[sessions show]] prints them
  (filters and limit), or the records are given by id.  Records of
  one query and filters on several providers are retired together.
  A merged record from before searches were recorded per provider has
  the query [[q | q]], which [[--query q]] does not match; such a
  record is picked by its id.
\item[[[--record]]] The ids [[sessions show]] prints, repeatable, each
  as a prefix of at least four characters.  The id is a digest of the
  record's key, so it names the same search after an append or a
  re-run, which reorder the records.
\item[[[--all-failed-outright]]] Every record of a search that failed
  without a single paper or was skipped ([[failed_outright]]), the
  malformed attempts and dead providers that make up most of the
  failures a caption counts.  Like reset's [[--source]], this is a
  filter: a second run finds nothing to do, which is not an error.
\end{description}
[[--undo]] clears the mark of the selected records instead; its
[[--note]] and [[--by]] would have nowhere to go, so they are refused
with it.  The note is stored on one line ([[retire_record]] collapses
its white space), and a [[--note]] of white space only is refused, as
it would record no reason.  A selected record that already is what the run would make
it (retired, or current under [[--undo]]) is named and left alone, so
that the first retirement's time and note stay.

<<sessions command>>=
@sessions_app.command("retire-search")
def sessions_retire_search(
    name: Annotated[
        str,
        typer.Argument(
            help="Session name or query whose search records to retire.",
            autocompletion=complete_session_name,
        ),
    ],
    query: Annotated[
        Optional[str],
        typer.Option(
            "--query",
            help="Select the records of this exact query. Never matches "
                 "a merged record (query `q | q`); use --record.",
        ),
    ] = None,
    provider: Annotated[
        Optional[str],
        typer.Option(
            "--provider", "-p",
            help="With --query: only the records of this provider.",
        ),
    ] = None,
    filters_like: Annotated[
        Optional[str],
        typer.Option(
            "--filters-like",
            help="With --query: only the records whose flags, as "
                 "`sessions show` prints them, contain this text.",
        ),
    ] = None,
    record_ids: Annotated[
        Optional[list[str]],
        typer.Option(
            "--record",
            help="Select a record by the id `sessions show` prints in "
                 "brackets (a digest of its query, provider and filters, "
                 "so it stays with the search), or a unique prefix of at "
                 "least 4 characters. Repeatable.",
        ),
    ] = None,
    all_failed_outright: Annotated[
        bool,
        typer.Option(
            "--all-failed-outright",
            help="Select every search that failed without a paper or "
                 "was skipped.",
        ),
    ] = False,
    undo: Annotated[
        bool,
        typer.Option(
            "--undo",
            help="Make the selected searches current again.",
        ),
    ] = False,
    dry_run: Annotated[
        bool,
        typer.Option(
            "--dry-run",
            help="Print what would change; write nothing.",
        ),
    ] = False,
    note: Annotated[
        Optional[str],
        typer.Option(
            "--note",
            help="Why the searches are retired, kept with each record.",
        ),
    ] = None,
    by: Annotated[
        Optional[str],
        typer.Option(
            "--by",
            help="Who retired the searches, kept as given (nothing is "
                 "recorded without it).",
        ),
    ] = None,
) -> None:
    """
    Retire search records, so that reports count the current searches.

    A retired search stays in the session with its papers and their
    links; `sessions show`, the report and the audit table count the
    current searches and state the retired ones apart. Running the
    search again with `-n` makes it current again. A Scholar older than
    this command drops the mark when it saves the session.

    Select records by --query (exact, narrowed by --provider and
    --filters-like; it never matches a merged record, query `q | q`),
    by --record (the ids `sessions show` prints in brackets, a digest
    of query, provider and filters that stays with the search), or
    with --all-failed-outright. A --query or --record that matches
    nothing saves nothing (exit 1). The session file is copied to
    `<name>.json.pre-retire-search-<time>.bak` before it is saved;
    --dry-run writes nothing.

    Examples:
        scholar sessions show my-review
        scholar sessions retire-search my-review --record 3fa9 \\
            --note "first version of the query"
        scholar sessions retire-search my-review --all-failed-outright \\
            --note "malformed" --dry-run
        scholar sessions retire-search my-review --query "q" --undo
    """
    from scholar.review import (
        RECORD_ID_MIN_PREFIX, SessionFileError, _utcnow, failed_outright,
        keep_copy_before_run, records_with_id_prefix, retire_record,
        save_session,
    )

    console = Console()
    <<validate retire-search options>>
    try:
        session = open_session_argument(name, strict=True)
    except SessionFileError as error:
        exit_on_unreadable_session(error)
    if session is None:
        console.print(f"[red]Session not found: {escape(name)}[/red]")
        raise typer.Exit(1)
    <<select the search records to retire>>

    chosen = [
        record for record in selected
        if (record.retired is not None) == undo
    ]
    state = "current" if undo else "retired"
    for record in selected:
        if record not in chosen:
            console.print(
                f"[yellow]{_record_line(record)} is already "
                f"{state}.[/yellow]"
            )
    verb = ("Would make" if dry_run else "Made") if undo else (
        "Would retire" if dry_run else "Retired"
    )
    target = " current" if undo else ""
    console.print(
        f"{verb} {len(chosen)} search record(s){target} in session "
        f"'{escape(name)}':"
    )
    for record in chosen:
        console.print(f"  {_record_line(record)}")
    if dry_run or not chosen:
        return
    copy = keep_copy_before_run(session, "pre-retire-search")
    at = _utcnow().isoformat(timespec="seconds")
    for record in chosen:
        if undo:
            record.retired = None
        else:
            retire_record(record, at, note, by)
    save_session(session)
    if copy is not None:
        console.print(f"[dim]Copy of the session before: {copy}[/dim]")
@

A record is named as [[sessions show]] names it, number, provider,
query and flags, so that the two outputs can be read side by side.

<<sessions command>>=
def _record_flags_text(record) -> str:
    """The flags of a search record as `sessions show` prints them."""
    return " ".join(_search_flags(record.filters, record.limit))


def _record_line(record) -> str:
    """A search record as `sessions show` lists it, escaped for Rich."""
    flags = _record_flags_text(record)
    query = record.query + (f" {flags}" if flags else "")
    return f"{escape(f'[{record.record_id}]')} " \
        f"{escape(_record_provider_label(record))}: {escape(query)}"
@

The options are checked before the session is loaded: exactly one way
of selecting, [[--provider]] and [[--filters-like]] only with
[[--query]], and no [[--note]] or [[--by]] with [[--undo]].

