The id names the search, not its place: [[create_review_session]] puts
the records of a new run first, so an append and a re-run between
[[sessions show]] and the command move every record, and the id must
still pick the search that was listed.  A prefix shared by two records
is refused, naming both; two such queries are found by trying names,
since the ids of invented queries are fixed but not chosen.  A note
over several lines is kept on one.

