@

\subsection{Agreement between screeners}
\label{sec:sessions-agreement}

[[sessions agreement]] reports how often the screeners of a session
agreed (\url{https://github.com/dbosk/scholarcli/issues/253}): for
each pair of screeners who screened the same records, a table of their
verdicts with its measures, for each of the three questions, kept or
discarded, bearing on the claim, and the category
(\cref{agreement-module} defines the measures and says why these and
no others).  It reads the screenings recorded with [[sessions screen]]
and the snapshots of the decisions taken with them, and writes
nothing.

Several sessions can be given; their records are counted side by side,
and a screener is the same screener in two sessions when kind and name
are spelled alike.  [[--pair A,B]] restricts the report to one pair, in
that order (A gives the rows), each named as [[kind:name]] or by kind
alone for the unnamed one, as the report prints them.  A pair whose
form cannot be read is a usage error (status~2) before any session is
loaded.

[[--sample ID]] reports over the papers of a stored review sample only
(\cref{sec:agreement-samples} in the agreement module): the sample's
papers in the sessions given and in the other sessions it pooled,
which are read from the files the sample recorded, as its own report
reads them ([[pooled_sample_sessions]]).  For a random sample the
observed agreement gets its 95\,\% interval; a stratified sample, named
by its group id, gives one block per band.  A sample none of the
sessions holds is a usage error (status~2), the ids they do hold
listed.

<<sessions command>>=
@sessions_app.command("agreement")
def sessions_agreement(
    names: Annotated[
        list[str],
        typer.Argument(
            help="Sessions whose screenings to compare (names or queries).",
            autocompletion=complete_session_name,
        ),
    ],
    sample: Annotated[
        Optional[str],
        typer.Option(
            "--sample",
            help="Only the papers of this stored review sample (its id, "
                 "or a stratified sample's group id), with a 95% "
                 "interval for the observed agreement.",
        ),
    ] = None,
    pair: Annotated[
        Optional[str],
        typer.Option(
            "--pair",
            help="Only this pair of screeners, as A,B, each kind:name "
                 "(or the kind alone for an unnamed screener).",
        ),
    ] = None,
    output_format: Annotated[
        str,
        typer.Option(
            "--format", "-f",
            help="Output format: table or json.",
            autocompletion=complete_display_format,
        ),
    ] = "table",
) -> None:
    """
    Report how often the screeners of a session agreed.

    For each pair of screeners with records in common: the table of
    their verdicts, observed agreement, positive and negative agreement
    and Cohen's kappa with the prevalence and bias indices, for kept or
    discarded and for bearing on the claim; the table and observed
    agreement for the four categories. No verbal label is given for
    kappa, and an interval only over a stored random sample.
    """
    from scholar.agreement import screener_verdicts
    from scholar.review import session_file_path

    console = Console()
    <<parse the [[--pair]] option>>
    sessions = []
    for name in names:
        session = open_session_argument(name)
        if session is None:
            console.print(f"[red]Session not found: {escape(name)}[/red]")
            raise typer.Exit(1)
        if all(session_file_path(session) != session_file_path(s)
               for s in sessions):
            sessions.append(session)
    if sample is not None:
        <<report the agreement over a sample>>
    else:
        <<report the agreement over every record>>
@

The pair is parsed by the agreement module's [[parse_screener_pair]]
(\cref{sec:agreement-screeners}), which splits it where a name cannot
continue and whose message names what is wrong.

<<parse the [[--pair]] option>>=
from scholar.agreement import parse_screener_pair

wanted = None
if pair is not None:
    try:
        wanted = parse_screener_pair(pair)
    except ValueError as error:
        console.print(
            f"[red]--pair {escape(pair)}: {escape(str(error))}[/red]",
            soft_wrap=True,
        )
        raise typer.Exit(2)
@

Over every record, the records are the decisions with screenings, each
read once ([[screener_verdicts]]); the pairs are those the records
hold, or the one asked for.  The text is built whole and printed once.

<<report the agreement over every record>>=
from scholar.agreement import (
    screener_pairs, screener_profiles, unknown_origin_count,
)

decisions = [d for s in sessions for d in s.decisions if d.screenings]
records = [screener_verdicts(d) for d in decisions]
profiles = screener_profiles(records)
pairs = [wanted] if wanted else screener_pairs(records)
blocks = [agreement_pair(records, profiles, a, b) for a, b in pairs]
unknown = unknown_origin_count(decisions)
if output_format == "json":
    print(json.dumps({"sample": None, "pairs": [b[1] for b in blocks],
                      "unknown_origin": unknown}, indent=2))
    return
lines = []
for text, _ in blocks:
    lines += text + [""]
if not blocks:
    lines.append("No two screeners have screened the same record.")
if unknown:
    lines.append(f"{unknown} verdict(s) of unknown origin not compared.")
print("\n".join(lines).rstrip("\n"))
@

[[agreement_pair]] gives a pair's lines and numbers: the header, then
a block per question.  A screener the asked pair names but no record
holds gets an empty profile, so the header says it screened nothing.

<<sessions command>>=
def agreement_pair(records, profiles, a, b, band=None):
    """The lines and the JSON of one pair's three questions.

    With `band` (a `SampleBand`), the tables are counted over the band
    with the interval where it applies.
    """
    from scholar.agreement import (
        QUESTIONS, ScreenerProfile, agreement_block, agreement_data,
        band_agreement, interval_withheld, pair_header, records_in_common,
        screener_data, screening_agreement,
    )

    profile_a = profiles.get(a) or ScreenerProfile(a)
    profile_b = profiles.get(b) or ScreenerProfile(b)
    both = records_in_common(records, a, b)
    lines = pair_header(profile_a, profile_b, both)
    data = {"a": screener_data(profile_a), "b": screener_data(profile_b),
            "both": both, "questions": []}
    for question in QUESTIONS:
        if band is None:
            table = screening_agreement(records, a, b, question)
            note = None
        else:
            table = band_agreement(band, a, b, question)
            note = interval_withheld(table, band)
        lines += agreement_block(table, interval_note=note)
        data["questions"].append(
            agreement_data(table, sample=band is not None)
        )
    return lines, data
@

Over a sample, each band is one block: the band (its confidence range,
for a band of a stratified sample), how many papers were drawn, how
many are counted, and how many were reset since the draw or not found,
then the pairs of that band's records.

<<report the agreement over a sample>>=
from scholar.agreement import (
    sample_bands, screener_pairs, screener_profiles,
)
from scholar.llm_review import confidence_criteria_text, pooled_sample_sessions

bands = sample_bands(pooled_sample_sessions(sessions), sample)
if not bands:
    held = sorted({s.sample_id for x in sessions for s in x.llm_samples})
    console.print(
        f"[red]--sample {escape(sample)} names no review sample of these "
        "sessions"
        + (f" (they hold {escape(', '.join(held))})" if held
           else " (they hold none)") + ".[/red]",
        soft_wrap=True,
    )
    raise typer.Exit(2)
lines, data = [], []
for band in bands:
    criteria = band.criteria
    title = f"Sample {band.sample_id}"
    if criteria.get("stratum"):
        title += ", confidence " + confidence_criteria_text(
            criteria.get("min_confidence"), criteria.get("max_confidence"),
            bool(criteria.get("no_confidence")),
        )
    lines += [
        title,
        f"  {band.size} papers drawn, {band.counted} counted, "
        f"{band.reset_since_draw} reset to pending since the draw and "
        f"{band.not_found} not found (left out)",
    ]
    profiles = screener_profiles(band.records)
    pairs = [wanted] if wanted else screener_pairs(band.records)
    entry = {"sample_id": band.sample_id, "census": band.census,
             "drawn": band.size, "counted": band.counted,
             "reset_since_draw": band.reset_since_draw,
             "not_found": band.not_found, "pairs": []}
    for a, b in pairs:
        text, numbers = agreement_pair(band.records, profiles, a, b, band)
        lines += text
        entry["pairs"].append(numbers)
    if not pairs:
        lines.append("  No two screeners have screened the same paper.")
    lines.append("")
    data.append(entry)
if output_format == "json":
    print(json.dumps({"sample": sample, "bands": data}, indent=2))
    return
print("\n".join(lines).rstrip("\n"))
@

