\subsection{Listing the screening conflicts}
\label{sec:sessions-conflicts}

[[sessions conflicts]] lists the papers on which two screeners
disagree (\cref{sec:agreement-conflicts} in the agreement module):
status conflicts, where one kept and the other discarded, and category
conflicts, where both gave the same status but different categories.
Each paper is listed with its id, which [[sessions decide --paper-id]]
takes, each screener's verdict, category and reason (cut like the
agent's reason in [[sessions show]]), and the outcome: the decision's
status and category, and whether a human has resolved the conflict by
deciding the paper after the screenings.  Adjudicating is deciding:
in the TUI (whose filter [[x]] lists the unresolved conflicts) or with
[[sessions decide --source human]], which record the human's decision;
nothing else is stored for it.

Above the list the command counts the papers in conflict as
[[sessions show]] does ([[conflict_counts]]: a paper with a status
conflict counts there, one with category conflicts only as
\enquote{category only}), and, for each pair
of screeners and kind of conflict, how the resolved ones came out:
equal to the first screener's verdict, to the second's, or to neither.
[[--pair]] lists one pair's conflicts only, [[--status-only]] and
[[--category-only]] one kind (not both: status~2), and
[[--unresolved]] only those no human has resolved.

