\paragraph{In [[sessions show]].}
[[sessions show]] says in a few lines what the two commands above
report: one line per pair with the records both screened, the observed
agreement on kept or discarded, kappa and the pair's status conflicts,
then one line counting the papers in conflict
([[ScreeningOverview]], \cref{sec:agreement-text} in the agreement
module); [[-f json]] gives the numbers under [[double_screening]].  The
lines are computed once, before the display and the JSON, and printed
in one call, not one per paper: printing is what makes [[sessions
show]] slow on large sessions
(\url{https://github.com/dbosk/scholarcli/issues/273}).  A session
without screenings gets neither the lines nor the key, so its display
and JSON stay as they were.

