\subsection{A model the [[llm]] package does not know}
\label{sec:cli-unknown-model}

A mistyped [[--model]] is a common mistake, and every LLM command ends
it with the same line and status~1: the model's name as the [[llm]]
package reports it and how to list the models it knows
([[resolve_llm_model]], \cref{sec:resolve-llm-model}).  Before, the
package's [[UnknownModelError]], a [[KeyError]], went past the
commands' [[ValueError]] clauses and ended [[llm classify]] and
[[llm synthesize]] in a traceback
(\url{https://github.com/dbosk/scholar/issues/284}).

The tests run the commands with the real [[llm]] package whose model
registries are emptied, as in the utilities' tests, so the error is the
package's own, class and message.  A command that ends in an uncaught
exception leaves it in [[result.exception]] (the runner catches it and
prints no traceback), so the tests check that the command ended by
[[typer.Exit]], which the runner records as a [[SystemExit]], and that the
output ends with the one line.  The model's name is long enough for
the line to pass the runner's 80 columns, so that Rich would break it
in two unless the commands print it without wrapping.

<<test functions>>=
UNKNOWN_MODEL = "a-model-name-long-enough-to-wrap-a-line"
UNKNOWN_MODEL_LINE = (
  f"Error: Unknown model: {UNKNOWN_MODEL}; "
  "`llm models` lists the available models"
)


def empty_llm_registries(monkeypatch, tmp_path):
  """Make the real `llm` package know no model, without its plugins."""
  import llm

  monkeypatch.setenv("LLM_USER_PATH", str(tmp_path / "llm"))
  monkeypatch.setattr(llm, "get_model_aliases", lambda: {})
  monkeypatch.setattr(llm, "get_async_model_aliases", lambda: {})
  return llm


def assert_unknown_model_line(result):
  """The command ended with the one line of an unknown model."""
  assert result.exit_code == 1, result.output
  assert isinstance(result.exception, SystemExit), result.exception
  assert "Traceback" not in result.output
  assert result.output.strip().splitlines()[-1] == UNKNOWN_MODEL_LINE


