def print_withheld_papers(
    console, session, withheld: list, lead: str = "Left pending"
) -> None:
    """List the papers the classifier left pending, grouped by reason.

    `lead` begins each heading; a second screen, which leaves no paper
    pending, says that no screening was stored instead.
    """
    from scholar.notes import get_paper_id

    titles = {
        get_paper_id(d.paper): d.paper.title for d in session.decisions
    }
    for heading, withheld_here in (
        ("no usable answer", [d for d in withheld if d.answer_problem]),
        ("no single category that fits the decision",
         [d for d in withheld if not d.answer_problem]),
    ):
        if not withheld_here:
            continue
        console.print(
            f"[yellow]{lead}, {heading} "
            f"({len(withheld_here)}):[/yellow]"
        )
        for decision in withheld_here:
            title = titles.get(decision.paper_id, decision.paper_id)
            console.print(
                f"  {escape(title)} [dim]({escape(decision.paper_id)}: "
                f"{escape(decision.problem)})[/dim]"
            )
@

[[scholar rq]] classifies its results with the same classifier
(\cref{sec:research-questions}), so it can leave papers pending for the same
reasons; it lists them with the same function, after its summary.

The classifier also withholds the decision of a paper whose answer is
unusable (\cref{sec:llm-parse} in the LLM review module): no answer,
a decision it cannot read, a missing or out-of-range confidence.
Those are listed under their own heading, because the remedy differs:
a category problem is about the vocabulary, an unusable answer about
the model, and the next batch may well answer it.

The summary reaches the user even though the other decisions of the
batch were applied and saved:

