\subsection{The classifier as second screener}
\label{sec:llm-classify-second-screen}

[[llm classify --second-screen]] runs the classifier over papers that
are already decided and records each answer as a screening beside the
decision, never as a decision ([[second_screen_with_llm]],
\cref{sec:second-screen} in the LLM review module, where the selection,
the blind prompt and the record are explained).  It is an option of
[[llm classify]] rather than a command of its own because everything
else is the classifier's: the model options, the batch size [[-n]], the
enrichment, the full-text passages, the vocabulary options and the
dry run mean what they mean for pending papers, and a second screen
should differ from the first in which papers it sees, not in how it
asks.  The papers are chosen with exactly one of [[--over all]],
[[--over machine]] or [[--sample ID]] for a review sample; there is no
default, because a second screen of every decided paper costs what the
first screen cost and should be chosen, not fallen into.
[[--rescreen]] lets the model screen again what it has screened since
the last reset.  Like the ordinary run, a second screen may fill a
missing abstract before it asks (unless [[--no-enrich]]); that is saved
with the screenings and changes the paper's record, not the decision.

