\paragraph{Classifying a first tier.}
\label{sec:llm-classify-tier}
The first tier a screen sheet can list (\cref{sec:sheet-tier}) can be
given to the classifier as well: [[--top K]] and
[[--min-providers N]] classify only the pending papers that meet
either condition, selected by the same [[screening_tier]] (\cref{sec:screening-tier} in
the review module), so that the tier a human screens from a sheet and
the tier a model classifies are the same papers.  The run prints the
counts of what the tier leaves, as the sheet does, before it
classifies the first [[-n]] papers of the tier; the papers it leaves
stay pending.  A second screen selects decided papers by its own
options and is refused with these.  The classifier hands the tier to
[[classify_papers_with_llm]] as its candidates, which keeps the pending
ones among them in session order; the examples and the vocabulary are
the session's as in an ordinary run.

