The summary counts the verdicts recorded and the papers they are on,
like [[sessions screen]]'s, and says that no decision was changed,
since the run looks like a classification (a filled abstract is a
change of the paper's record, which the help states).  A screen by the model that
made the decision is announced on a line of its own, so that nobody
reads it as an independent screener without being told.  The papers
skipped are counted, each with its cause, and the number left to screen
lets a script repeat the run until it reaches zero.  Withheld answers
are listed as the ordinary run lists them, under a heading that says
